{"id":"n4_u01_l1","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"Verbs for states and activities","goal":"Learn 15 verbs you will use with ～ています.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_sumimasu","v_tsutomemasu","v_shirimasu","v_mochimasu","v_kaburimasu","v_hakimasu","v_kakemasu","v_naraimasu","v_utaimasu","v_oyogimasu","v_hashirimasu","v_arukimasu","v_araimasu","v_okurimasu","v_owarimasu"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Verbs of living, working, wearing","body":["すみます (live), つとめます (work for), しります (get to know), もちます (carry), かぶります / はきます / かけます (wear on the head / feet / eyes), ならいます (learn), うたいます (sing), およぎます (swim), はしります (run), あるきます (walk), あらいます (wash), おくります (send), おわります (end)."],"examples":[{"ja":"めがね を かけています","reading":"megane o kakete imasu","en":"I am wearing glasses."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_vb01","q_n4u01_vb02","q_n4u01_vb03","q_n4u01_vb04","q_n4u01_vb05","q_n4u01_vb06","q_n4u01_vb07","q_n4u01_vb08","q_n4u01_vb09","q_n4u01_vb10","q_n4u01_vb11","q_n4u01_vb12","q_n4u01_vb13","q_n4u01_vb14","q_n4u01_vb15","q_n4u01_ty01","q_n4u01_ty02","q_n4u01_ty03"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_vb01","q_n4u01_vb03","q_n4u01_vb05","q_n4u01_vb08","q_n4u01_vb10","q_n4u01_vb14","q_n4u01_ty01"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l2","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"People, school and work words","goal":"Name people, work and school things.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_kaisha","v_gaikoku","v_otokonohito","v_onnanohito","v_nimotsu","v_shukudai","v_shiken","v_jugyou","v_meeru","v_pasokon","v_puuru","v_michi"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Useful nouns","body":["かいしゃ (company), がいこく (foreign country), おとこのひと / おんなのひと, にもつ, しゅくだい, しけん, じゅぎょう, メール, パソコン, プール."],"examples":[{"ja":"パソコン を つかっています","reading":"pasokon o tsukatte imasu","en":"I am using a computer."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_ty04","q_n4u01_ty05","q_n4u01_vm_kaisha","q_n4u01_vm_gaikoku","q_n4u01_vm_otokonohito","q_n4u01_vm_onnanohito","q_n4u01_vm_nimotsu","q_n4u01_vm_shukudai","q_n4u01_vm_shiken","q_n4u01_vm_jugyou","q_n4u01_vm_meeru","q_n4u01_vm_pasokon","q_n4u01_vm_puuru","q_n4u01_vm_michi"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_ty04","q_n4u01_ty05"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l3","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"Order and time words","goal":"Say first, next, finally, already, not yet and later.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_mazu","v_sorekara","v_tsugini","v_saigoni","v_mou","v_mada","v_atode","v_zutto"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Words that organise a story","body":["まず (first), それから (and then), つぎに (next), さいごに (finally), もう (already), まだ (not yet), あとで (later), ずっと (all along)."],"examples":[{"ja":"まず て を あらって、それから ごはん を たべます","reading":"mazu te o aratte sorekara gohan o tabemasu","en":"First wash your hands, and then eat."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_ty06","q_n4u01_ty07","q_n4u01_dc04","q_n4u01_vm_mazu","q_n4u01_vm_sorekara","q_n4u01_vm_tsugini","q_n4u01_vm_saigoni","q_n4u01_vm_mou","q_n4u01_vm_mada","q_n4u01_vm_atode","q_n4u01_vm_zutto"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_ty06","q_n4u01_ty07","q_n4u01_dc04"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l4","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"Linking actions with て","goal":"Say several actions in order.","introduces":{"grammar":["g_te_sequence"]},"explain":[{"heading":"て, て, ます","body":["Join actions with the て-form; only the last verb takes ます or ました. Use まず, それから, つぎに and さいごに to show the order."],"examples":[{"ja":"あさ おきて、ごはん を たべて、がっこう へ いきます","reading":"asa okite, gohan o tabete, gakkou e ikimasu","en":"I get up, eat, and go to school."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gs01","q_n4u01_gs02","q_n4u01_gs03","q_n4u01_gs04","q_n4u01_gs05","q_n4u01_gs06","q_n4u01_gs07","q_n4u01_tf01","q_n4u01_tf02","q_n4u01_tf03","q_n4u01_tf04","q_n4u01_tf05","q_n4u01_tf06","q_n4u01_tf07","q_n4u01_tf08","q_n4u01_tf09","q_n4u01_tf10"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gs01","q_n4u01_gs02","q_n4u01_gs03","q_n4u01_gs05","q_n4u01_tf01","q_n4u01_tf05","q_n4u01_tf06"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l5","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"～ています","goal":"Say what you are doing and what state you are in.","introduces":{"grammar":["g_te_iru"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Doing and being","body":["て-form + います is \"is doing\" (およいでいます) or a continuing state (すんでいます, かけています, つとめています)."],"examples":[{"ja":"とうきょう に すんでいます","reading":"toukyou ni sunde imasu","en":"I live in Tokyo."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gi01","q_n4u01_gi02","q_n4u01_gi03","q_n4u01_gi04","q_n4u01_gi05","q_n4u01_gi06","q_n4u01_gi07","q_n4u01_gi08","q_n4u01_tr01","q_n4u01_tr02","q_n4u01_tr03","q_n4u01_tr04","q_n4u01_tr05","q_n4u01_tr06","q_n4u01_tr07","q_n4u01_gl01","q_n4u01_gl02","q_n4u01_gl03","q_n4u01_gl04","q_n4u01_dc01","q_n4u01_dc02"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gi01","q_n4u01_gi02","q_n4u01_gi03","q_n4u01_gi04","q_n4u01_gi05","q_n4u01_tr01","q_n4u01_gl02","q_n4u01_dc01"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l6","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"～てから, もう and まだ","goal":"Say what happens after, and what is already done or not yet done.","introduces":{"grammar":["g_te_kara","g_mou_mada"]},"explain":[{"heading":"After doing","body":["て-form + から means \"after\". もう ... ました is \"already\"; まだ ... ていません is \"not yet\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"まだ ごはん を たべていません","reading":"mada gohan o tabete imasen","en":"I have not eaten yet."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gk01","q_n4u01_gk02","q_n4u01_gk03","q_n4u01_gk04","q_n4u01_gk05","q_n4u01_gk06","q_n4u01_gm01","q_n4u01_gm02","q_n4u01_gm03","q_n4u01_gm04","q_n4u01_gm05","q_n4u01_gm06","q_n4u01_tr08","q_n4u01_tr09","q_n4u01_tr10","q_n4u01_gl05","q_n4u01_gl06","q_n4u01_gl07","q_n4u01_gl08","q_n4u01_dc03"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_gk01","q_n4u01_gk02","q_n4u01_gk04","q_n4u01_gm01","q_n4u01_gm02","q_n4u01_gm03","q_n4u01_gl05"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n4_u01_l7","unit_id":"n4_u01","instructional_level":"N4","title":"Kanji: 会 社 国 外 子 女 男 手","goal":"Read eight kanji for people, places and the hand.","introduces":{"kanji":["k_kai","k_sha","k_koku","k_gai","k_ko","k_onna","k_otoko","k_te"]},"explain":[{"heading":"People and places","body":["会 (meet) and 社 (company) make 会社. 国 (country) and 外 (outside) make 外国. 子 is a child, 女 a woman, 男 a man, 手 a hand."],"examples":[{"ja":"会社","reading":"kaisha","en":"company"},{"ja":"外国","reading":"gaikoku","en":"foreign country"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_kd01","q_n4u01_kd02","q_n4u01_kd03","q_n4u01_kd04","q_n4u01_kd05","q_n4u01_kd06","q_n4u01_kd07","q_n4u01_kd08","q_n4u01_kk01","q_n4u01_kk02","q_n4u01_kk03","q_n4u01_kk04","q_n4u01_kk05","q_n4u01_kk06","q_n4u01_kk07","q_n4u01_kk08","q_n4u01_kmt01","q_n4u01_kcf01","q_n4u01_kcf02"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n4u01_kd01","q_n4u01_kd03","q_n4u01_kd06","q_n4u01_kd07","q_n4u01_kk01","q_n4u01_kk02","q_n4u01_kk05","q_n4u01_kmt01"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
